09c68510cbd382541bf2827aba6b" commit="4f84699384115bf9aa00c5f3df78565197226f5b" commit_message="vboot: Fix potential alignment issue reading FWMP  RollbackFwmpRead() assumed that a uint8[] array on the stack would be aligned sufficiently for typecasting to struct RollbackSpaceFwmp and accessing its members.  This was true on x86 (where unaligned accesses work fine) and probably harmless on other platforms (since RollbackSpaceFwmp is __attribute__(packed).  But it's cleaner to switch to using a union of the buffer and struct, since that will provide the proper alignment.  BUG=chromium:601492 BRANCH=baytrail and newer platforms TEST=make -j runtests  Change-Id: I97077923ab5809c68510cbd382541bf2827aba6b Signed-off-by: Randall Spangler &lt;rspangler@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362087 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Daisuke Nojiri &lt;dnojiri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="362087" owner_email="rspangler@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/vboot_reference" ref="refs/changes/87/362087/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I3569b167674ad9fb98588c829abad67efdfeb1d3" commit="b32357dc10078daff82f868f5518e6a0c4b098f7" commit_message="Cross-compilation fixes and improvements  Corresponds to r1476 from upstream Compilation now uses target OS detection instead of host OS. If target OS/architecture is unknown, the Makefile will complain. Format string warnings on DJGPP have been disabled.  (from upstream log): Native and cross-compilation now usually just require setting CC. Examples: make CC=i586-pc-msdosdjgpp-gcc make CC=&quot;clang -m64&quot; make CC=i686-w64-mingw32-gcc  BUG=chromium:478356 BRANCH=none TEST=compiled locally, but needs testing targeted at CC.  Change-Id: I3569b167674ad9fb98588c829abad67efdfeb1d3 Signed-off-by: Souvik Ghosh &lt;souvikghosh@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/358961 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: David Hendricks &lt;dhendrix@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="358961" owner_email="souvikghosh@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/flashrom" ref="refs/changes/61/358961/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie9d4341e7c2429f7e6ced43b5c08cd2e7024a715" commit="55049332d007367aff512aa768b9d75132e0df56" commit_message="FROMLIST: chromiumos-overlay: import ath10k fimrware 10.2.4.70.54  Import ath10k firmware 10.2.4.70.54 until it is available on linux-firmware.  Here are the change lists between 70.52 and 70.54 (from QCA): ----------------------------------------------------------------- CL#1540748 Issue 54903 in chrome-os-partner: ath10k FW should not generate WMI STA KICK OUT event for SA training frames. Bypass the sta kick out for training packets in FW.  CL#1544024 Smart antenna flag is not defined for utf. Protect it with smart antenna compilation macro. Otherwise this would result in UTF failure. ----------------------------------------------------------------------  BUG=b:30277091 TEST=Run basic test on Arkham. MacBook Pro is associated with Arkham at HT20/2G and VHT80/5G. 2G and 5G throughput is normal in OTA test.  Change-Id: Ie9d4341e7c2429f7e6ced43b5c08cd2e7024a715 Signed-off-by: Yixiang Li &lt;yixiang@google.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362401 Reviewed-by: Srinivasa duvvuri &lt;sduvvuri@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="362401" owner_email="yixiang@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/01/362401/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I31b2d501b5e7977f24e580fe06f00f54d9cf2805" commit="7f482f198e540dcb8f90d510c7d0e3cb4a3bbdac" commit_message="Store mobmonitor logs in /mnt/moblab/tmp &amp; restrict file list  BUG=chromium:589170 TEST=local moblab  Change-Id: I31b2d501b5e7977f24e580fe06f00f54d9cf2805 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/329336 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Matthew Sartori &lt;msartori@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="2" gerrit_number="329336" owner_email="msartori@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/chromite" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/chromite" ref="refs/changes/36/329336/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="2"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I06071b08641334838e2cf17c8a3292b463ceef96" commit="ada9f1261f83d718c67267af42bfb9b5cb33c358" commit_message="Fixed the type &quot;secrete&quot;.  BUG=chromium:630482 TEST=Manual.  Change-Id: I06071b08641334838e2cf17c8a3292b463ceef96 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362447 Commit-Ready: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362447" owner_email="ntang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/47/362447/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="If77f887e1dd14981985d1665bdb76ee81f330196" commit="33736459592edc61753ccd1d2abd2d228547cda1" commit_message="Enable tko protobuffer export by generating the proto python client code.  BUG=chromium:626371 TEST=Manually tested.  Change-Id: If77f887e1dd14981985d1665bdb76ee81f330196 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360902 Commit-Ready: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Simran Basi &lt;sbasi@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Michael Tang &lt;ntang@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="360902" owner_email="ntang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="4" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/02/360902/4" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="Id94c94881f170091cd56bf2aef7fe0d759492ba7" commit="4eebe03189ca292372d6f5fad373b424aabe5060" commit_message="CHROMIUM: arm64: dts: remove duplicate touchpad pinctrl reference for gru  This pinctrl node is claimed by both the i2c5 bus node (rk3399-gru.dtsi) and the trackpad@4a node (rk3399-gru-kevin.dtsi). The latter is misplaced.  Fixes these errors:  [    3.629863] rockchip-pinctrl pinctrl: pin gpio3-12 already requested by ff140000.i2c; cannot claim for 5-004a [    3.629875] rockchip-pinctrl pinctrl: pin-108 (5-004a) status -22 [    3.629889] rockchip-pinctrl pinctrl: could not request pin 108 (gpio3-12) from group ap-i2c-tp-pu-en  on device rockchip-pinctrl [    3.629898] atmel_mxt_ts 5-004a: Error applying setting, reverse things back  BUG=none TEST=boot kevin; don't see the above errors; touchpad still works  Change-Id: Id94c94881f170091cd56bf2aef7fe0d759492ba7 Signed-off-by: Brian Norris &lt;briannorris@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362477 Reviewed-by: Douglas Anderson &lt;dianders@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362477" owner_email="briannorris@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/77/362477/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ib932e02f15bd1aad7811032a12d826c76476e53f" commit="334c80a0fdf9f8ac37397874e81d27e073ffde8b" commit_message="Cr50: NvMem: Modified nvmem_init to handle 2 corrupt partitions  During initialization the NvMem module looks for either a valid partition or that the NvMem area is fully erased. If neither of these two conditions were found, then it was only returning an error code and logging a message to the console.  This CL modifies nvmem_init() so that if the error case as described above is detected, then it will call nvmem_setup() which will create two valid partitions. In addition, the setup function erases all of the existing data in the NvMem space.  Enhanced the unit test that deals with both partitions being corrupted so that it verifies the version numbers are correct and that all user buffer data is set to 0xff.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:55536 BRANCH=None TEST=Manual Executed make runtests TEST_LIST_HOST=nvmem and verifed that all tests passed.  Change-Id: Ib932e02f15bd1aad7811032a12d826c76476e53f Signed-off-by: Scott &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362448 Commit-Ready: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Scott Collyer &lt;scollyer@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362448" owner_email="scollyer@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/ec" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/ec" ref="refs/changes/48/362448/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I731eab542e095e3c5b43e194374cf891bf302426" commit="fa33d926bf73e476df033c970a12bb7d23aa491e" commit_message="Make component registration atomic, and check version rollback.  This changes makes the component registration atomic, so that when updating a component, a crash does not leave the component in a bad state. This is accomplished by having generational folders of a component and a symlink that is atomically updated to point at the most recent.  BUG=chromium:588220 TEST=emerge imageloader and run the test client with the test data CQ-DEPEND=CL:361410,CL:361584  Change-Id: I731eab542e095e3c5b43e194374cf891bf302426 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/361560 Commit-Ready: Greg Kerr &lt;kerrnel@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Greg Kerr &lt;kerrnel@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Ricky Zhou &lt;rickyz@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="361560" owner_email="kerrnel@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="6" project="chromiumos/platform/imageloader" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/imageloader" ref="refs/changes/60/361560/6" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I032ed0c6ce5d9518e278982419254a020b3d8617" commit="23e373c260fd0367e289504ff4da48965233a2aa" commit_message="power_SuspendStress: increase daily run to 250 iterations.  BUG=chromium:626467 TEST=manual, atest -m &lt;dut&gt; --control-file power_SuspendStress/control.bareDaily 'foo' completes successfully.  Change-Id: I032ed0c6ce5d9518e278982419254a020b3d8617 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362124 Commit-Ready: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Puneet Kumar &lt;puneetster@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="362124" owner_email="tbroch@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/24/362124/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-3.18" change_id="Ie5d05a84c17c9c65c63c421e2c8f871814123168" commit="f3d9e9d562bbc9447d9751d33b6b833e5954384c" commit_message="CHROMIUM: drm/i915: Count flip/mode_set errors on crtcs  In intel_crtc, store the number of flip or mode_set errors (well, some of them, for now), and expose them via debugfs.  BUG=chromium:627618 TEST=Compiles  Change-Id: Ie5d05a84c17c9c65c63c421e2c8f871814123168 Signed-off-by: Sean Paul &lt;seanpaul@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/360431 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Todd Broch &lt;tbroch@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="360431" owner_email="seanpaul@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/31/360431/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I16e6885a4e40c78e81d9bbc42c9af79e5f55047e" commit="d23d3dc174e6cb57ed2633a9609eb45766f08fb4" commit_message="g: deactivate the PHY during usb_release  The USB controller should disable the PHY itself when usb is released, but from the power tests I ran it does not. This change adds a call in usb_release to deactivate the PHY.  It looks like having the AP on vs off also makes a difference in power consumption. I am looking into that now, but until that is resolved turn of the AP off while testing this USB change to see the effects on power.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:54331 BRANCH=none TEST=manual  Without deactivating the PHY put cr50 into deep sleep on gru.  run 'reboot ap-off'  measure pp3300_haven_mw and it is around 4.5mW  Add deactivating the PHY during usb_release.  Put cr50 into deep sleep  run 'reboot ap-off'  measure the power and the average should be around 2mW  Change-Id: I16e6885a4e40c78e81d9bbc42c9af79e5f55047e Signed-off-by: Mary Ruthven &lt;mruthven@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/362159 Commit-Ready: Dan Shi &lt;dshi@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Bill Richardson &lt;wfrichar@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="362159" owner_email="m